## Hierarchical production decision engine

Use `scripts/hierarchical_inference.py` instead of directly treating the PyTorch
score as the final business decision:

```bash
python src/scripts/hierarchical_inference.py \
  --checkpoint artifacts/best.pt \
  --master data/master_entities.csv \
  --relationships data/entity_relationships.csv \
  --query "Jhonson & Jhonson" \
  --json
```

The decision order is:

`EXACT → APPROVED_ALIAS → FORMER_NAME/DBA/SAME_LEGAL_ENTITY → RELATED_ENTITY(REVIEW) → FUZZY_MATCH → REVIEW → NO_MATCH`

Every decision contains an explainable `reason_code` and `evidence` object.
The engine intentionally does not treat a parent, subsidiary, or affiliate as the
same legal entity.

See `docs/hierarchical_decision_engine.md`.
